<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-hidden-order" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Lens of Representation: Uncovering Hidden Order</title>
  <introduction>
    Many of the most profound ideas in science are rooted in taking on new perspectives to think about
    physical systems that already have a well-established conventional representation. The <alert>big ideas</alert>
    do not emerge from changes in the physical system themselves (nor the methods used to observe and measure them), but rather
    newfound understandings that reveal hidden structures in nature.
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="before-and-after-boltzmann.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="information-pipeline.ptx"/>

</section>